  <docinfo>
    <macros>
    \newcommand{\R}{\mathbb{R}}
    </macros>
    <latex-image-preamble>
    \usepackage{tikz}
    </latex-image-preamble>
  </docinfo>

  <article xml:id="math-major-advising">
    <title>Mathematics Major Advising</title>
    <subtitle>Santa Clara University, Department of Mathematics and Computer Science</subtitle>

    <introduction>
      <p>
        The <xref ref="ch-planner" text="title"/> and the
        <xref ref="ch-cs-planner" text="title"/> take what a student has completed
        and lay out the rest of the major quarter by quarter, with warnings for
        anything that cannot wait, and print a copy of the plan. The
        <xref ref="ch-maps" text="title"/> and <xref ref="ch-cs-map" text="title"/>
        show each major on one page, with every prerequisite drawn as an arrow. The
        <xref ref="ch-requirements" text="title"/> and
        <xref ref="ch-cs-requirements" text="title"/> sections restate the degree
        requirements from the 2026<ndash/>27 Undergraduate Bulletin, which is the
        source for everything else here.
      </p>
      <p>
        The Bulletin does not say which quarter each course is offered in, or which
        years the alternate-year courses fall on. The planner ships with placeholder
        offerings; the department's actual rotation should be entered in the
        offerings table in the planner, and the file <c>assets/planner.html</c>
        should be updated so the placeholders match.
      </p>
    </introduction>

    <xi:include href="ch-planner.ptx"/>
    <xi:include href="ch-cs-planner.ptx"/>
    <xi:include href="ch-maps.ptx"/>
    <xi:include href="ch-cs-map.ptx"/>
    <xi:include href="ch-requirements.ptx"/>
    <xi:include href="ch-cs-requirements.ptx"/>

  </article>
</pretext>
